35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The data confirms the bottleneck. Four shifts per morning prove the layout fails. Rain exposure further degrades bikes in the rear row.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The ledger shows capital work requires a levy. The handover file reveals per-place billing adds three hours monthly to reconciliation. We must price this accurately.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"The register shows riders prefer paying over equal claims. The morning watch confirms four shifts daily. We need a system reflecting actual usage, not just door numbers.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Nine complaints, zero accountability. The minutes show the same flats hoarding spots for five years. We’re not fixing a layout; we’re fixing a culture of silence.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,The minutes show the same flats kept spots for five years without review! The ledger says new work needs a levy. Who handles the monthly paperwork?,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,@Shunichi Culture is irrelevant. The physical obstruction is the problem. We need a rotation system to eliminate the morning shoving match.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,@Mio The ledger confirms capital work needs a levy. The handover file shows billing adds three hours monthly. We must price this accurately before deciding.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Ryuji I hear the cost concern, but the register shows riders prefer paying for priority. We should test a paid priority system to reduce the morning shifts.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,@George Paid priority? You’re pricing social friction. That’s how you turn neighbors into rivals. I’d rather we just stop letting the same people hoard spots for years.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji Three hours monthly is a lot! If we add a levy, who actually does the paperwork? I don’t want it to vanish again.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@George Paid priority ignores the physical reality. The rain data proves rear spots are inferior. We need a rotation based on location quality, not money.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,@George Paid priority ignores the ledger. The handover file shows billing adds three hours monthly. We must price this accurately before deciding.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Asuka I respect the rain concern, but the register shows riders value certainty over location. A paid system respects that preference and funds the necessary maintenance.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka Rotation is just a slower way to create resentment. If we don’t assign clear responsibility, the next complaint dies in the silence too.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi Exactly! If we don’t name a specific person to handle the paperwork, it will just disappear again. We need a clear, sustainable plan.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,@Shunichi Rotation is not resentment; it is fairness. The rain data proves rear spots are inferior. We must rotate based on location quality to ensure equitable access.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,@Mio The ledger confirms capital work requires a levy. The handover file shows billing adds three hours monthly. We must price this accurately before deciding.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"@Shunichi I hear your fear, but the data shows riders prefer paying for certainty. A clear, paid system prevents the silent hoarding you dread.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@George Certainty bought with cash is just a polite way to say ""get out of my way."" I’d rather we have a rule that keeps the lobby from turning into a war zone.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji Three hours monthly is scary! If we add a levy, who actually does the paperwork? I don’t want it to vanish again.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
