60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option B. Open racks eliminate the morning shoving match and the rain exposure issue. No fixed spots means no hoarding, no rotation resentment, and no financial burden.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option A. The ledger shows capital work requires a levy. Option B ignores the financial reality. We must price the infrastructure accurately before committing.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,Option A. The register shows riders prefer paying for certainty. This funds maintenance and stops the silent hoarding I fear.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option C. A lottery is blind and fair. It stops the hoarding without turning the lobby into a marketplace. Let’s keep it simple and human.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option C! A lottery is simple and fair. No monthly paperwork to vanish, no money to manage. Just a yearly draw!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji Option B requires no new infrastructure, so your ledger concerns are irrelevant. The physical flow is the only metric that matters here.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,@Asuka The ledger shows capital work requires a levy. Option B ignores the financial reality. We must price the infrastructure accurately before committing.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"@Shunichi I understand your preference for simplicity, but the data shows riders value certainty. A lottery leaves them anxious about losing their spot, which fuels the very resentment we fear.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,@George Anxiety is just uncertainty. A lottery is a clean break. It stops the hoarding without turning us into a marketplace.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@George But if the lottery winner moves out, does the spot just sit empty? I worry about the paperwork to track that!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio If a resident leaves, the space simply returns to the pool. No tracking, no paperwork. Option B is the only solution that respects the physical reality.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,@Mio The ledger confirms capital work requires a levy. Option B ignores the financial reality. We must price the infrastructure accurately before committing.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,@Mio The spot returns to the pool. But riders prefer certainty. A lottery creates anxiety. Option A respects their preference for stability and funds maintenance.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mio The spot returns to the pool. No tracking, no paperwork. Option C is the only one that doesn’t turn our lobby into a marketplace.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi I’m worried! If the spot returns to the pool, who updates the list? I don’t want to be the one doing that paperwork every month!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio There is no list to update. Option B has no assigned spaces. The racks are open to everyone. No tracking, no paperwork, no burden.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,@Mio The ledger confirms capital work requires a levy. Option B ignores the financial reality. We must price the infrastructure accurately before committing.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,"@Mio The list updates only once a year. Option A provides the certainty riders want, preventing the anxiety and resentment I fear.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mio It’s one name change a year, not a monthly audit. Stop worrying about paperwork and let’s keep the lobby from becoming a war zone.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Mio,,@Shunichi One name change a year is manageable! I’ll take that over. Option C it is!,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
